  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Frontier Technologies &#x2013; ODA: Using New Technologies to Tackle Global Challenges and Improve Lives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports the UK&#x2019;s international development objectives by enabling responsible use of emerging technologies to improve the lives of people in poverty. It helps FCDO staff and partners design, test, and scale innovative solutions to global challenges such as climate change, disability inclusion, and access to essential services. Activities include real-world experimentation, capacity building, and research to strengthen local ecosystems and promote equitable technology adoption. The project aims to benefit 8 million people in developing countries and leverages &#xa3;5 million in co-funding to support early-stage ideas. All activities align with the Sustainable Development Goals and promote inclusive, ethical, and locally relevant innovation. The project also contributes to strengthening FCDO&#x2019;s internal innovation capacity and supports the Foreign Secretary&#x2019;s ambition to modernise development through technology.</narrative>
  </description>
